Subject: [PATCH] Build the standalone i2pd daemon on Android (DaemonUnix)

FoxHole execs i2pd as a child process (packaged as libi2pd.so, like libTor.so),
not as the JNI library the Android target defaults to. Under -DANDROID the daemon
collapses to the DaemonAndroid stub (no start/stop/run, no gracefulShutdownInterval),
so daemon/UnixDaemon.cpp fails to compile. Defining ANDROID_BINARY selects the real
DaemonUnix while leaving the rest of i2pd's Android behaviour intact.

--- a/build/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/build/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -180,6 +180,13 @@ if(UNIX)
   list(APPEND DAEMON_SRC "${DAEMON_SRC_DIR}/UnixDaemon.cpp")
   if(NOT(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "OpenBSD" OR APPLE))
     # "'sleep_for' is not a member of 'std::this_thread'" in gcc 4.7/4.8
     add_definitions("-D_GLIBCXX_USE_NANOSLEEP=1")
   endif()
+  # FoxHole runs i2pd as a standalone exec'd process (like libTor.so), not the JNI library the
+  # Android target defaults to. Under -DANDROID the daemon collapses to the DaemonAndroid stub
+  # (no start/stop/run), so UnixDaemon.cpp fails to compile. Defining ANDROID_BINARY selects the
+  # real DaemonUnix while keeping the rest of i2pd's Android behaviour intact.
+  if(ANDROID)
+    add_definitions("-DANDROID_BINARY")
+  endif()
 endif()

--- a/daemon/HTTPServer.cpp
+++ b/daemon/HTTPServer.cpp
@@ -1306,6 +1306,28 @@ namespace http {
 			}
 		}
 
+		if (req.uri == "/foxhole-status")
